Package: LLMTranslate
Title: 'shiny' App for TRAPD/ISPOR Survey Translation with LLMs
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jonas R.", "Kunst", , "jonas.r.kunst@bi.no", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Athanasia M.", "Mowinckel", , "a.m.mowinckel@psykologi.uio.no", role = "ctb",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5756-0223", GitHub = "drmowinckels"))
  )
Description: A 'shiny' application to automate forward and back survey
    translation with optional reconciliation using large language models
    (LLMs). Supports both item-by-item and batch translation modes for
    optimal performance and context-aware translations. Handles
    multi-sheet Excel files and supports OpenAI (GPT), Google Gemini,
    Anthropic Claude, and many other providers via the 'ellmer' package.
    Follows the TRAPD (Translation, Review, Adjudication, Pretesting,
    Documentation) framework and ISPOR (International Society for
    Pharmacoeconomics and Outcomes Research) recommendations. See Harkness
    et al. (2010) <doi:10.1002/9780470609927.ch7> and Wild et al.  (2005)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1524-4733.2005.04054.x>.
